{"id":"8537052fa5cec8c4","group":"58","path":"58/batch12/58-df-cofinality-spectrum.md","title":"Cofinality Spectrum","display":"df-cofinality-spectrum — Cofinality Spectrum","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-cofinality-spectrum","aliases":["58-df-cofinality-spectrum"],"display":"df-cofinality-spectrum — Cofinality Spectrum","depends_on":["[[58-df-pcf]]","[[58-df-regular-cardinal]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-cofinality-spectrum"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-cofinality-spectrum</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-cofinality-spectrum — Cofinality Spectrum"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b82cea6742372d50\" href=\"?note=b82cea6742372d50\" title=\"58-df-pcf\">58-df-pcf</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"58-df-regular-cardinal\">58-df-regular-cardinal</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A,P\">\\(A,P\\)</span> (ZFC object variables for the family and its spectrum)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\\)</span> (regular-cardinal predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"58-df-regular-cardinal\">58-df-regular-cardinal</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{pcf}\">\\(\\operatorname{pcf}\\)</span> (possible-cofinalities operator, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"b82cea6742372d50\" href=\"?note=b82cea6742372d50\" title=\"58-df-pcf\">58-df-pcf</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CofinalitySpectrum}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{CofinalitySpectrum}_S\\)</span> (cofinality spectrum predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}cofinality\\text{-}spectrum} \\vdash \\mathrm{CofinalitySpectrum}_S(A,P)\\leftrightarrow A\\neq\\emptyset\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in A\\;\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land|A|&lt;\\min(A)\\land P=\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}cofinality\\text{-}spectrum} \\vdash \\mathrm{CofinalitySpectrum}_S(A,P)\\leftrightarrow A\\neq\\emptyset\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in A\\;\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land|A|&lt;\\min(A)\\land P=\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The spectrum is the canonical <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\">\\(\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\\)</span> set from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"b82cea6742372d50\" href=\"?note=b82cea6742372d50\" title=\"58-df-pcf\">58-df-pcf</a>, with the progressive-set side condition stated explicitly.</li>\n<li>Shelah's theorem: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda^{\\mathrm{cf}(\\lambda)} = \\sum_{\\kappa \\in \\mathrm{pcf}(\\lambda)} \\lambda^{&lt;\\kappa}\">\\(\\lambda^{\\mathrm{cf}(\\lambda)} = \\sum_{\\kappa \\in \\mathrm{pcf}(\\lambda)} \\lambda^{&lt;\\kappa}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The pcf structure controls cardinal exponentiation at singular cardinals.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-pcf","status":"resolved","id":"b82cea6742372d50","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-pcf]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-regular-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"0fbfc19800246e77","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-regular-cardinal]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-regular-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"0fbfc19800246e77","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S$ (regular-cardinal predicate, see [[58-df-regular-cardinal]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-pcf","status":"resolved","id":"b82cea6742372d50","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{pcf}$ (possible-cofinalities operator, see [[58-df-pcf]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-pcf","status":"resolved","id":"b82cea6742372d50","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Remark]","excerpt":"The spectrum is the canonical $\\operatorname{pcf}(A)$ set from [[58-df-pcf]], with the progressive-set side condition stated explicitly.","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"A,P","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{pcf}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CofinalitySpectrum}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}cofinality\\text{-}spectrum} \\vdash \\mathrm{CofinalitySpectrum}_S(A,P)\\leftrightarrow A\\neq\\emptyset\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in A\\;\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land|A|<\\min(A)\\land P=\\operatorname{pcf}(A)","display":true},{"tex":"\\operatorname{pcf}(A)","display":false},{"tex":"\\lambda^{\\mathrm{cf}(\\lambda)} = \\sum_{\\kappa \\in \\mathrm{pcf}(\\lambda)} \\lambda^{<\\kappa}","display":false}],"bytes":1221,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-308","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-cofinality-spectrum.md|58-df-cofinality-spectrum]]（batch12）"}],"outgoing":["b82cea6742372d50","0fbfc19800246e77"]}